<title>NETHERLANDS: ING Barings maintains KLM as a sell.</title>
<headline>ING Barings maintains KLM as a sell.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1997-02-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Summary of Feb 5 research.</p>
<p>Company---------Sector--------Price---Broker----------------</p>
<p>KLM		 airline	 55.60   ING Barings</p>
<p>COMMENT: SELL maintained. KLM's Q3 96/97 results revealed the company's true operating situation as the net profit was no longer inflated by accounting effects. We are still concerned about the development of unit costs versus yield. Company is still negotiating with unions regarding &quot;Focus 2000&quot; reorganisation. KLM's operating results a bottoming-out between now and Q2 97/98, excluding the effect of fuel cost rises, but only slowly. Stock is worth about 50 guilders.</p>
<p>    Estimates (Dfl):   EPS     P/E Dividend</p>
<p>    1995/96 (actual)   5.86     9.3    2.00</p>
<p>    1996/97		4.40    12.4    1.75</p>
<p>    1997/98		3.80    14.4    1.50</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom, +31 20 504 5000 (Fax +31 20 504 5040)</p>
